    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "TSPSC exams frequently question the origins of Perini Shivatandavam under Kakatiya patron Ganapati Deva and its modern revival by Padmashri Nataraja Ramakrishna.",
        "Geographical Indication (GI) tags associated with Telangana textiles and handicrafts (e.g., Pochampally Ikat, Cheriyal Paintings, Bidriware) are high-priority topics.",
        "Key literary figures of Telangana across Telugu and Urdu traditions (such as Bammera Pothana, Dasarathi, and Muhammad Quli Qutb Shah) are repeatedly asked in competitive exams."
      ],
      "id": "mui86cm"
